# No PWA / Not Installable

The owner explicitly does not want the marketing site to behave like an installable app.

- `src/app/manifest.ts` MUST keep `display: "browser"`. Never change it to `standalone`, `minimal-ui`, or `fullscreen`.
- NEVER add a service worker, `next-pwa`, Workbox, offline caching, or an install prompt/banner of any kind.
- NEVER add `beforeinstallprompt` handlers or "Add to Home Screen" UI.
- The manifest exists only for brand identity signals (name, icons, colors). If a change would make Chrome show an install prompt, it violates this rule.

Note: this restriction is about the marketing site (my-app) only. The merchant portal is a separate app with its own decisions.
